      "value": "@{5ab3ad272b67505f726c2a8f|full_name}: I think you're at least partially right since it does take a few hours to start up and that would point to a video memory leak by the game.  My 1080Ti has 11GB.  Things that seem to point to something else though are the fact that (at least for me) it ONLY ever happens after using Virtual Desktop, AND once it starts happening if i open the steam overlay I can see the game being rendered perfectly smoothly underneath the overlay.  Closing the Steam overlay (which should theoretically free up some VRAM) causes the game to go back to a powerpoint framerate.  I think there is something else going on here, possibly in addition to a memory leak.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
