      "value": "@{5ecf1097bd4f840563673fd6|full_name}: The reason I knew it was a vram issue is because I also have the 1080ti. 11GB isnt going to save anyone. When it comes to opening the steamvr menu and everything working fine it is because the game is not rendering at full resolution behind the overlay so it will only cause an issue when you come back out of the overlay in most cases when your vram is full. Yes there is a possible memory leak involved with opening and closing the overlays but its not as noticeable when compared to how much avatars and mirrors will use. This vram issue is common because things such as just sitting in a public world will have plenty of unoptimised avatars  loading in and out eating your vram.\nLast I saw in regards to clearing unused vram you need to load two new worlds. Even then it never clears everything so eventually the game will reach max and require a restart. \nYou have a strong enough system to run something like hwinfo. I use it to warn me when my vram reaches 95% so I have time to restart the game before I run into any issues.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
