      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I only began to get this issue a few days ago, right when VR Input Emulator was installed (prerequisite for VRPlayspaceMover). Could have been a coincidence, and maybe VRChat is responsible due to an issue with the current update. But VRPlayspaceMover does add its own UI buttons to the SteamVR panel that comes up when looking at the desktop in VR, so it is tied in there. And you said Oculus launcher works fine. If you use VRPlayspaceMover too, it might have some issue causing this. Probably began with the new SteamVR update we just got, if not the VRChat build then this could be the cause.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
