      "value": "@{5a69eccdd20e79665351e7c1|full_name}: If people are only getting it in more recent times then that does add some suspicious regarding more recent updates for anything used to play vrchat. As for input emulator, its possible but it would not be a combination of recent updates and you installing it because this vram issue has been around for years. \nIf vrchat ever figures out what is wrong with the oculus cv1 crashes I may be able to test the theory surrounding the oculus version not  having vram issues, but until then I cant confirm it being purely an issue on steamvr.",
