  "details": "Playing on Oculus Rift S through SteamVR.  The issue has been happening for at least a couple weeks now, and usually occurs after playing for more than an hour.  When accessing my virtual desktop through either the SteamVR overlay or the Oculus Virtual Desktop, VRChat will run unplayably slow when returning to the game.  It doesn't seem to matter which method I use to access my desktop, either way will trigger the issue.  The actual fps looks like low single digits and it's impossible to do anything in game.  If I open the SteamVR overlay, the game suddenly start running at 80fps behind the overlay.  But if I go back into the game, it starts running terribly again.  I usually have to relaunch the game entirely to fix it.\n\nI have a fairly powerful PC and the game runs fine otherwise.  I also don't seem to encounter this issue if I play the game through the Oculus app, but then I lose the ability to use my Vive trackers.  i7-8700k, 32gb RAM, 1080Ti.",
